ai-agent",\n  "timestamp": "2025-01-16T00:00:00Z",\n  "summary": {\n    "total_findings": 12,\n    "critical": 3,\n    "high": 3,\n    "medium": 6,\n    "low": 0,\n    "info": 0\n  },\n  "dimensions": {\n    "frontmatter": {\n      "score": 0,\n      "max": 20,\n      "findings": [\n        {\n          "severity": "CRITICAL",\n          "code": "FM-001",\n          "title": "No SKILL.md file present",\n          "description": "The agentskills.io specification requires a SKILL.md file at the root of the skill directory with YAML frontmatter. This system is a full application, not a skill.",\n          "remediation": "Create a SKILL.md file with proper YAML frontmatter (name, description, license, metadata, allowed-tools) if this is intended to be published as a skill."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "CRITICAL",\n          "code": "FM-002",\n          "title": "No YAML frontmatter structure",\n          "description": "Required fields missing: name, description, license, metadata, allowed-tools. The system lacks the structured metadata required by the specification.",\n          "remediation": "Add YAML frontmatter to SKILL.md with all required fields."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "CRITICAL",\n          "code": "FM-003",\n          "title": "No skill name validation",\n          "description": "Cannot validate skill name against folder name, character restrictions, or length limits (1-64 chars, [a-z0-9_-]+).",\n          "remediation": "Define a skill name in YAML frontmatter and ensure it matches the parent folder name."\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "structure": {\n      "score": 7,\n      "max": 20,\n      "findings": [\n        {\n          "severity": "HIGH",\n          "code": "ST-001",\n          "title": "Non-compliant directory structure",\n          "description": "Project uses application-centric structure (mcp_servers/, evaluation/, tests/) instead of skill-centric structure (scripts/, references/, assets/). No separation of core instructions from supplementary documentation.",\n          "remediation": "Reorganize as: SKILL.md (core), references/ (detailed specs), scripts/ (utilities), assets/ (templates)."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "MEDIUM",\n          "code": "ST-002",\n          "title": "Monolithic agent definitions",\n          "description": "All agent logic, MCP initialization, and execution flow are in agents.py and main.py. No modular skill structure.",\n          "remediation": "Break agents.py into separate skill modules: email-skill/, sql-skill/, drive-skill/, etc., each with its own SKILL.md."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "MEDIUM",\n          "code": "ST-003",\n          "title": "Missing reference documentation",\n          "description": "No references/ directory with detailed specifications, error handling guides, or integration patterns.",\n          "remediation": "Create references/ with: delegation-patterns.md, error-handling.md, tool-contracts.md, mcp-protocol.md."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "MEDIUM",\n          "code": "ST-004",\n          "title": "Evaluation pipeline outside skill scope",\n          "description": "evaluation/ directory contains RAG testing and RAGAS metrics, but these are not part of the skill definition.",\n          "remediation": "Move evaluation/ to a separate testing/benchmarking repository or document it as a separate skill."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "LOW",\n          "code": "ST-005",\n          "title": "Frontend assets not organized",\n          "description": "index.html and script.js are at the root; should be in assets/ or frontend/ directory.",\n          "remediation": "Create assets/frontend/ and move UI files there."\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "disclosure": {\n      "score": 5,\n      "max": 20,\n      "findings": [\n        {\n          "severity": "CRITICAL",\n          "code": "PD-001",\n          "title": "No progressive disclosure — monolithic loading",\n          "description": "All agents, MCP servers, and tool definitions are loaded at startup via lifespan context manager. No conditional loading of reference files or supplementary documentation.",\n          "remediation": "Implement conditional loading: SKILL.md defines core instructions; reference files are loaded only when specific conditions are met (e.g., \'if user asks about error handling, load references/error-handling.md\')."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "MEDIUM",\n          "code": "PD-002",\n          "title": "No explicit trigger conditions for reference files",\n          "description": "README.md is comprehensive but not structured as conditional references. No clear \'when to read\' guidance for supplementary documentation.",\n          "remediation": "Add conditional triggers to SKILL.md: \'Read references/delegation-patterns.md if evaluating multi-agent architectures\' or \'Read references/tool-contracts.md if implementing a new specialist agent\'."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "MEDIUM",\n          "code": "PD-003",\n          "title": "SKILL.md body would exceed 500 lines if created",\n          "description": "The README.md is ~800 lines. If converted to SKILL.md, it would violate the line limit for core instructions.",\n          "remediation": "Condense SKILL.md to <500 lines; move detailed architecture, use cases, and API reference to references/."\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "architecture": {\n      "score": 8,\n      "max": 20,\n      "findings": [\n        {\n          "severity": "HIGH",\n          "code": "AR-001",\n          "title": "Missing architecture rationale document",\n          "description": "No explicit justification for: (1) Supervisor pattern choice, (2) 7 specialist agents, (3) Gemini 2.0 Flash selection, (4) MCP protocol adoption, (5) HITL safety design.",\n          "remediation": "Create references/architecture-rationale.md documenting design decisions, trade-offs, and complexity justifications."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "HIGH",\n          "code": "AR-002",\n          "title": "Supervisor agent scope is too broad",\n          "description": "The Supervisor agent has 14 tools (6 read, 8 write) and makes all routing decisions. This violates the principle of focused responsibility. A true specialist should have 2-4 tools max.",\n          "remediation": "Refactor: Create a Router agent (routes to specialists) and keep Supervisor for synthesis only. Or split Supervisor into domain-specific orchestrators (EmailOrchestrator, DataOrchestrator, etc.)."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "MEDIUM",\n          "code": "AR-003",\n          "title": "Missing explicit tool contracts",\n          "description": "Each tool (send_email, query_database, etc.) lacks documented input/output schemas. Tool expectations are implicit in agent prompts.",\n          "remediation": "Create references/tool-contracts.md with JSON schemas for each tool: inputs (required/optional fields, types), outputs (success/error payloads), side effects, and HITL requirements."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "MEDIUM",\n          "code": "AR-004",\n          "title": "Error handling strategy is ad-hoc",\n          "description": "No systematic error recovery policy. Confirmation flow handles HITL, but tool failures, timeouts, and retries are not documented.",\n          "remediation": "Document error handling in references/error-handling.md: (1) Tool failure modes, (2) Retry logic, (3) Fallback strategies, (4) User notification patterns."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "MEDIUM",\n          "code": "AR-005",\n          "title": "No ADLC evidence for production-grade system",\n          "description": "Missing: (1) Problem statement, (2) Scope definition, (3) Anticipated failure modes, (4) Evaluation criteria, (5) Success metrics.",\n          "remediation": "Create references/adlc-design.md documenting: problem statement, agent responsibilities, input/output contracts, failure modes, and evaluation metrics (latency, accuracy, cost)."\n        },\n        {\n          "severity": "MEDIUM",\n          "code": "AR-006",\n          "title": "Delegation pattern not explicitly validated",\n          "description": "While no circular dependencies are detected, the delegation flow (Supervisor → Specialists → MCP → APIs) is not formally documented or validated.",\n          "remediation": "Create references/delegation-patterns.md with: (1) Delegation flow diagram, (2) Non-overlapping responsibility matrix, (3) Data flow contracts, (4) Circular dependency checks."\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  "top_gaps": [\n    "No SKILL.md file with YAML frontmatter — system is not agentskills.io-compliant",\n    "No progressive disclosure — all agents/tools loaded at startup, no conditional reference loading",\n    "Supervisor agent scope too broad (14 tools) — violates focused responsibility principle",\n    "Missing architecture rationale document — design decisions not explicitly justified",\n    "Missing tool contracts — input/output schemas not documented",\n    "Missing ADLC evidence — no problem statement, failure modes, or evaluation criteria",\n    "No error handling strategy — tool failures and retries are ad-hoc",\n    "Directory structure is application-centric, not skill-centric"\n  ],\n  "top_fixes": [\n    "1. Create SKILL.md with YAML frontmatter (name: \'vertical-ai-agent\', description, license, metadata, allowed-tools)",\n    "2. Reorganize directory structure: SKILL.md (core), references/ (detailed specs), scripts/ (utilities), assets/ (templates)",\n    "3. Condense SKILL.md to <500 lines; move detailed architecture to references/architecture-overview.md",\n    "4. Create references/architecture-rationale.md justifying Supervisor pattern, specialist count, and model selection",\n    "5. Create references/tool-contracts.md with JSON schemas for all 14 tools (inputs, outputs, HITL requirements)",\n    "6. Refactor Supervisor agent: split into Router (routing logic) + Synthesizer (response synthesis) to reduce scope",\n    "7. Create references/error-handling.md documenting failure modes, retry logic, and fallback strategies",\n    "8. Create references/delegation-patterns.md with delegation flow diagram and non-overlapping responsibility matrix",\n    "9. Add conditional loading triggers to SKILL.md: \'Read references/X.md if [condition]\'",\n    "10. Document ADLC evidence: problem statement, scope, anticipated failures, evaluation metrics"\n  ],\n  "recommendation": "block",\n  "rationale": "This is a production-grade multi-agent orchestration system, not an agentskills.io-compliant skill. It lacks the fundamental structure required by the specification: (1) no SKILL.md file, (2) no YAML frontmatter, (3) no progressive disclosure, (4) no skill-centric directory organization. While the architecture itself is sound (clear delegation, HITL safety, non-overlapping responsibilities), it cannot be published or distributed as a skill without significant restructuring. Recommendation: Either (A) refactor as a single \'vertical-ai-agent\' skill with proper SKILL.md and progressive disclosure, or (B) decompose into 7 separate skills (email-skill, sql-skill, drive-skill, etc.), each with its own SKILL.md and focused responsibility."\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**This system is architecturally sound but specification-incompatible.** It\'s a full application, not an agentskills.io skill. To make it compliant:\n\n1. **Create SKILL.md** with proper YAML frontmatter\n2. **Implement progressive disclosure** — move detailed specs to `references/`\n3. **Refactor Supervisor scope** — split into Router + Synthesizer\n4. **Document architecture rationale** — justify design decisions\n5. **Define tool contracts** — explicit input/output schemas\n6. **Add ADLC evidence** — problem statement, failure modes, metrics\n\nThe **recommendation is BLOCK** until these structural changes are made.', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}][0m[32;1m[1;3m
